  "mainEntity": {
    "name": "Why is My Drywall Bubbling?",
    "text": "Why is My Drywall Bubbling?",
    "@type": "Question",
    "answerCount": 1,
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "text": "Seeing bubbling paint or drywall can be a real head-scratcher and often signals a deeper issue than just a bad paint job. Usually, bubbling is caused by moisture. This could be anything from a leaky pipe behind the wall to high humidity, or even a roof leak letting water seep in from above. Before you even think about patching or repainting, you've got to find and fix that moisture source. Patching over an active leak or mildew problem is a huge mistake because the issue will just come right back, and possibly worse than before. You need to inspect the area carefully, maybe even checking for signs of mold or a damp smell. Once the moisture source is completely eliminated and the area is dry, then you can move on to repairing the surface. This involves removing the damaged section, applying new drywall or patching compound, sanding it smooth, priming, and finally painting to match. If you're unsure about the source of the moisture or the damage is extensive, it’s really important to call in a professional. HH Remodeling LLC can help with interior wear and tear repairs, including drywall issues, in the Denver area. Give us a call at 303-505-0866.",
      "@type": "Answer",
      "author": {
        "name": "HH Remodeling LLC",
        "@type": "Organization"
      }
    }
  }
